## Every list in the text report shows at most ten items and names at most
## three functions inline, then says how many more there are, since a large
## binary can have thousands of each. main calls into a cycle of twelve
## functions, each of which calls a function without a frame size, five of
## which call out of the file, and the last of which calls leaf. The file has
## eleven indirect call targets of unknown type.

# RUN: yaml2obj %s -o %t
# RUN: llvm-stack-size %t | FileCheck %s --match-full-lines

#      CHECK:Indirect call targets of unknown type:
# CHECK-NEXT:  t0 (0x5000)
# CHECK-NEXT:  t1 (0x5010)
# CHECK-NEXT:  t2 (0x5020)
# CHECK-NEXT:  t3 (0x5030)
# CHECK-NEXT:  t4 (0x5040)
# CHECK-NEXT:  t5 (0x5050)
# CHECK-NEXT:  t6 (0x5060)
# CHECK-NEXT:  t7 (0x5070)
# CHECK-NEXT:  t8 (0x5080)
# CHECK-NEXT:  t9 (0x5090)
# CHECK-NEXT:  and 1 more functions
# CHECK-EMPTY:
# CHECK-NEXT:Entry point: main (0x1000)
# CHECK-NEXT:  Stack usage: at least 464 bytes (lower bound)
# CHECK-NEXT:  Lower bound because:
# CHECK-NEXT:    cycle: c0 (0x2000), c1 (0x2010), c2 (0x2020) and 9 more
# CHECK-NEXT:    unknown frame size: u0 (0x3000)
# CHECK-NEXT:    unknown frame size: u1 (0x3010)
# CHECK-NEXT:    unknown frame size: u2 (0x3020)
# CHECK-NEXT:    unknown frame size: u3 (0x3030)
# CHECK-NEXT:    unknown frame size: u4 (0x3040)
# CHECK-NEXT:    unknown frame size: u5 (0x3050)
# CHECK-NEXT:    unknown frame size: u6 (0x3060)
# CHECK-NEXT:    unknown frame size: u7 (0x3070)
# CHECK-NEXT:    unknown frame size: u8 (0x3080)
# CHECK-NEXT:    unknown frame size: u9 (0x3090)
# CHECK-NEXT:    and 2 more functions without a frame size
# CHECK-NEXT:    unknown callees: <external> (0x0), called by c0 (0x2000), c1 (0x2010), c2 (0x2020) and 2 more
# CHECK-NEXT:  Max stack path:
# CHECK-NEXT:    main (0x1000): 16 bytes
# CHECK-NEXT:    c0 (0x2000): 32 bytes
# CHECK-NEXT:    c1 (0x2010): 32 bytes
# CHECK-NEXT:    c2 (0x2020): 32 bytes
# CHECK-NEXT:    c3 (0x2030): 32 bytes
# CHECK-NEXT:    c4 (0x2040): 32 bytes
# CHECK-NEXT:    c5 (0x2050): 32 bytes
# CHECK-NEXT:    c6 (0x2060): 32 bytes
# CHECK-NEXT:    c7 (0x2070): 32 bytes
# CHECK-NEXT:    c8 (0x2080): 32 bytes
# CHECK-NEXT:    c9 (0x2090): 32 bytes
# CHECK-NEXT:    and 2 more functions of this cycle with 64 more bytes
# CHECK-NEXT:    leaf (0x4000): 64 bytes

--- !ELF
FileHeader:
  Class:   ELFCLASS64
  Data:    ELFDATA2LSB
  Type:    ET_EXEC
  Machine: EM_AARCH64
  Entry:   0x1000
